## the synonym map, and why the column above is not the finding
The probes name their axes with the short symbols the corpus argues in.
dimension.toml names them with long descriptive slugs. So `w` reads as
undeclared against `integer_width` and `f` against `fraction_width`, and
the C2 arm below would have passed on that alone, which is the arm
cheating rather than finding anything. Nothing mechanical bridges the two
spellings, which is itself worth stating: no check can confirm that a
predicate naming `integer_width` corresponds to a probe that swept `W`.
The map below is hand-written and is a reading, not a measurement.

  w=integer_width
  f=fraction_width
  width=total_width
  policy=overflow_policy
  overflow=overflow_policy
  op=operation
  mode=rounding
  signed=signedness
  signedness=signedness
  rounding=rounding
  arity=arity
  operation=operation
  threads=threads
  container=container
  strategy=strategy
  alignment=alignment
  profile=build_profile
  optlevel=build_profile
  opt=build_profile
  lto=build_profile
  assertions=build_profile
  build=build_profile
  depth=chain_length
  steps=chain_length
  chain=chain_length

