## the toolchain, which is the residue arm worth a number
The pinned nightly is a condition on every compiled result in this
corpus and is not a declared axis. `build_profile` is the optimisation
settings; the compiler version is a different thing, and a result at one
nightly is not established at another.
probe directories:                        135
naming the pinned nightly anywhere:       49
C5 PASS: the count does not exceed its own population
C5 exists because a first hand-run of this count returned 202 of 135.
It split the path on the wrong field and counted directory names that
were not probe directories. A count exceeding its own denominator is the
cheapest control available and it is available on every count.

C3: a key here is not necessarily an axis. `differ` and `ops` are result
columns and appear in this list; nothing mechanical separates a parameter
from an output, so the distinct-value count above is the only signal and
the classification in the findings file is a reading rather than a count.
